# Security and governance (lightweight)

Align with common secure-development practice without heavy process:

- Secrets only via `.env` (gitignored) or Modal secrets; never hardcode.
- Least privilege: UI local; remote worker only receives generation params and needed bytes.
- Validate/sanitize paths from `models.txt` (no path traversal into unexpected dirs).
- Prefer HTTPS download URLs for models; skip or warn on cleartext if avoidable.
- Do not log prompts/images when `ZERO_TELEMETRY=true`.
- Dependency pins in requirements where practical; document notable upgrades in the audit log.
- Threat model stays simple: protect credentials, Volume contents, and accidental data retention.
